{"File":"/Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/04-analysis-fidelity.md","LineNumber":95,"LineContent":"fn rust_ast_symbols_include_signatures_impl_owner_and_trait_impl() {"}
{"File":"/Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/04-analysis-fidelity.md","LineNumber":100,"LineContent":"    //   new → impl_owner = Some(\"Widget\u003cT\u003e\"), trait_impl = None"}
{"File":"/Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/04-analysis-fidelity.md","LineNumber":101,"LineContent":"    //   render → impl_owner = Some(\"Widget\u003cT\u003e\"), trait_impl = Some(\"Render\")"}
{"File":"/Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/07-edge-cases-and-failure-modes.md","LineNumber":23,"LineContent":"**Naming mismatches that wouldn't compile.** Part 4 uses `impl_owner` throughout where Part 1/3's canonical `SymbolEntry` field is `owner` (04#1), and invents a `Visibility::Super` variant that doesn't exist in Part 1's four-variant enum (04#2). These aren't edge cases — they're the fidelity fixes failing to type-check against the structs they're supposed to extend."}
{"File":"/Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/07-edge-cases-and-failure-modes.md","LineNumber":136,"LineContent":"1. **`impl_owner` doesn't exist.** Part 4 uses this field name throughout (header, code identifiers, test description); Part 1's canonical `SymbolEntry` and Part 3's confirmed field list both say `owner`. Not a rename — just a different name for the same field, unreconciled."}
{"File":"/Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/README.md","LineNumber":24,"LineContent":"- See [07-edge-cases-and-failure-modes.md](./07-edge-cases-and-failure-modes.md) for the full list of undecided failure-mode behavior — none of it blocks starting implementation, but several findings (the `impl_owner`/`owner` and `Visibility::Super` mismatches in Part 4, in particular) should be resolved before writing the code they touch."}

